# INVENTORY ONLY. Do not source this file or deploy its placeholders.
# GitHub Environment VARIABLES (staging / production separately):
# DEPLOY_ENV: inferred from protected branch name, staging or production
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL: https://staging.dartspoint.nl OR https://dartspoint.nl
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL: https://realtime.staging.dartspoint.nl OR https://realtime.dartspoint.nl
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: project-specific https://<ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: public client key, not secret/service_role
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY: environment-specific public CAPTCHA site key
# CAPTCHA secret: configure in Supabase Auth dashboard, never NEXT_PUBLIC or this VPS runtime
# NODE_IMAGE: compatible stable Node LTS image pinned by @sha256:<64 hex>
# REDIS_IMAGE: compatible stable Redis image pinned by @sha256:<64 hex>
# MAIL_FROM: DartsPoint <noreply@dartspoint.nl> (staging use isolated verified sender)
# MAIL_REPLY_TO: chosen monitored support mailbox
# GitHub Environment SECRETS:
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY: server only; never NEXT_PUBLIC, logs or browser artifacts
# DATABASE_URL: restricted application DB role; TLS; direct/session pooler
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL: separate privileged migrations role; TLS
# RESEND_API_KEY: server worker application mail (SMTP auth configured in Supabase separately)
# INTERNAL_DEPLOY_TOKEN: >=32 random bytes represented as safe ASCII, same current/next during deploy
# BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_EMAIL: explicit Nick owner address, not yet supplied; bootstrap-only secret
# Error monitoring / object-storage variables can be added when selected.
# Neither blank values nor example credentials are accepted by prepare-release.py.
